  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "20261122T131955Z-5ebdeccd#1",
      "line": 58,
      "path": "experiments/lean-code-store/lean_code_store/source.py",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The pinned Lean compiler accepts `deriving instance BEq,` followed by `Hashable for T` at the same indentation, but the extractor truncates the first instance’s text and stores only the class name for the second. Fix: Recognize continuation tokens through the end of the target list and add a test that both instances receive the same complete command text."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261122T131955Z-5ebdeccd#2",
      "line": 66,
      "path": "experiments/lean-code-store/lean_code_store/rows.py",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The new report is tested only on fresh rows, so `run` still accepts file versions written by the previous extractor and silently reuses counts that omit unresolved helpers. Fix: Bump `EXTRACTOR_VERSION` and test that a completed file version from the previous extractor is re-extracted."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261122T131955Z-5ebdeccd#3",
      "line": 29,
      "path": "plans/20261122-lean-code-store-prototype.status.md",
      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The status says the first prototype implemented the selected-module reporting rules, but its recorded run left 161 generated constants unnamed in addition to the 13,108 constants for which no rule matched. Fix: Record the 161 omissions in the first-run entry and identify the later reporting fix separately."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261122T131955Z-5ebdeccd#4",
      "line": 48,
      "path": "experiments/lean-code-store/fixture/Fixture/Types.lean",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The external-folding fixture still produces the expected `Nat` body and mention rows if the extractor drops `Nat.casesOn`, because `natCase` also refers directly to `Nat` in both contexts. Fix: Use a fixture where the generated constant is the sole source of the expected relationship to its parent."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261122T131955Z-5ebdeccd#5",
      "line": 41,
      "path": "experiments/lean-code-store/tests/test_clickhouse.py",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The query test passes if the distinct-user condition is removed because no target in the fixture has two named users and zero anonymous uses. Fix: Add a second named user of `c` alongside a first named user and assert that `a` remains the only result."
    }
